So I’d expect several kinds of music at once.

Fractal music. A motif unfolds into smaller versions of itself. Open one fold and hear a phrase; open farther and discover that phrase was one note in a larger phrase.

Palindromic music. Because folding creates natural reflection symmetry. Unfold one direction and get A\to B\to C; refold and get C\to B\to A. The physical operation becomes musical inversion/reversal.

Polyphonic music. Different folds could represent simultaneous layers. One crease unfolds rhythm, another harmony, another melody. Fully open it and formerly separated voices suddenly become one composition.

Context-sensitive music. The same crease means something different depending upon which neighboring folds are currently open. That’s very LLM-like:

Meaning(symbol)\neq constant

but rather:

Meaning(symbol\mid surrounding\ folds)

Generative music. There needn’t be one canonical song. Different unfolding routes produce different compositions while preserving the same underlying relational structure.

